# Line endings are decided HERE, not by each machine.
#
# WHY: core.autocrlf=true on Windows checks files out as CRLF while the blobs
# are LF. Git normalises CRLF->LF on read, so status/diff/write-tree ALL report
# clean -- but prettier compares real bytes and fails. That divergence hid a
# 183-file working-tree corruption that three git instruments called clean.
#
# text=auto: git decides what is text. eol=lf: text is checked out as LF on
# every platform, which is what prettier writes and what the blobs already hold.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
